#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   9696848
#=GF RT   Identification of specific nucleotide sequences within the conserved 3'-SL
#=GF RT   in the dengue type 2 virus genome required for replication.
#=GF RA   Zeng L, Falgout B, Markoff L
#=GF RL   J Virol 1998;72:7510-7522.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   8672458
#=GF RT   Evidence for the existence of a pseudoknot structure at the 3' terminus of
#=GF RT   the flavivirus genomic RNA.
#=GF RA   Shi PY, Brinton MA, Veal JM, Zhong YY, Wilson WD
#=GF RL   Biochemistry 1996;35:4222-4230.
#=GF CC   This family represents the Flavivirus 3'-SL cis-acting replication element
#=GF CC   (CRE). The family is thought to play a crucial role in replication and is
#=GF CC   thought to be needed for the formation of a "replication complex" [1].
#=GF CC   Although evidence has been presented for an existence of a pseudoknot
#=GF CC   structure in this RNA [2], it does not appear to be well conserved across
#=GF CC   flaviviruses. Deletions of the 3' UTR of flaviviruses have been shown to
#=GF CC   be lethal for infectious clones.
#=GF WK   Flavivirus
#=GF SQ   84

